    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "385dc419_900f9811",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ShaderCodeDictionary.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T19:33:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because if I\u0027m reading the original bug correctly, it is only safe to take the max of each coverage in certain cases and need to use min otherwise. Specifically:\n\n```\na \u003d lerp(da, a, max(cr, cg, cb))\n\nwhich is correct when (a - da) \u003e\u003d 0, but when (a - da) \u003c 0 the min should be used.\n```\n\nBut if we know source alpha is always opaque, then we know we\u0027ll always be in the first case and can use max.",
      "parentUuid": "72cc6833_8452bba5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 353,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 357,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "49fc6d0c8138f02fb835b2864ea4be4f46c9af6f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
